15 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542715 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542715 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d848745-0d69-5731-947e-0a9ae11809b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542962 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542962 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542962 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "79ac5216-69de-5dc4-a92b-b636df49e5d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542982 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542982 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542982 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f21a217-b4f0-55ce-b377-f084a5b14d24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543088 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543088 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543088 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa4333dc-3ea2-5e37-ab50-ec3e34c12a9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543150 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543150 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543150 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2c913d4-93f7-5765-8bb6-090f7d52622b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543157 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c588edce-5cf5-501a-93b4-d2734b483461" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543200 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543200 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543200 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "db2d98c7-af14-5f48-be6c-f11b82999c7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543210 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543210 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543210 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e014b07e-27e4-516d-adc5-1ef689408d39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186542962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543298 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0c3c93af-58f9-530c-baad-0a629ae81ede" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186542715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186543200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186543088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543407 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a29f2b28-9204-5899-8070-b3f5ffe02498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543482 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543482 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543482 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543482 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $3\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nII. Any $8\\times 6$ matrix $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543482 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e0723ce-a987-5c3e-a185-24b9f3aa7c5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543482 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $8\\times 6$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $6\\times 8$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $6\\times 6$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{6\\times 8}\\times {A}_{8\\times 6}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{6\\times 6}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $6$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have a negative singular value.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95283" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543511 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ has one negative singular value.\n\nII. Any $2\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. Any $6\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $6$ distinct singular values." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66207faf-3d6b-5406-8c58-c05d9d84a48f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543511 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have any negative singular value.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,  since $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 2}\\times {A}_{2\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $6\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 6}\\times {A}_{6\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
